--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
UPSTREAM ATTRIBUTION THAT TRAVELS WITH THESE FILES
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

Many files here contain values derived from third-party datasets that are
themselves CC BY 4.0. Redistributing these files carries their attribution
requirement as well as this one:

  * Materials Project (CC BY 4.0) -- material ids, formulas, space groups, hull
    distances and DFT energies; and structures relaxed from MP starting points.
    A. Jain et al., APL Materials 1, 011002 (2013). doi:10.1063/1.4812323

  * Matbench Discovery / WBM (CC BY 4.0) -- material identifiers.
    J. Riebesell et al., Nature Machine Intelligence (2025), arXiv:2308.14920.
    H.-C. Wang, S. Botti, M. A. L. Marques, npj Comput. Mater. 7, 12 (2021).

Changes were made: values were selected, re-binned, relabelled, and in some cases
used as the starting point for relaxations computed by this harness.

The root NOTICE file carries the full attribution block. data/README.md states,
file by file, which data is which.

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
EXCLUSIONS -- third-party material NOT licensed by this file
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

The following three files are NOT this project's to license. They are excluded
from the CC BY 4.0 grant above and remain subject to their own terms:

  data/experimental_lattice_constants.csv
      40 measured lattice constants transcribed from Table I of
      R. A. Lucero, T. M. Henderson, G. E. Scuseria,
      J. Phys.: Condens. Matter 24, 145504 (2012).
      doi:10.1088/0953-8984/24/14/145504 -- Copyright IOP Publishing.

  data/experimental_csonka2009.csv
      29 measured lattice constants transcribed from Table II of
      G. I. Csonka, J. P. Perdew et al., Phys. Rev. B 79, 155107 (2009).
      arXiv:0903.4037 -- Copyright American Physical Society.

  data/mbd_published.json
      Published leaderboard metrics from the model metadata files in the
      matbench-discovery repository, github.com/janosh/matbench-discovery,
      licensed MIT, Copyright (c) 2022 Janosh Riebesell. The full MIT notice is
      reproduced in the root NOTICE file.

See data/README.md for the reasoning behind each exclusion.
